READ THE p6/p10 ROWS AS WRITTEN. The four fast-preset gradient cells are
null-to-marginally-negative — three of the four spans straddle 1.0, and
`gradient 256 p10`'s does not (p25 0.9990), so that cell is a ~0.7 % SLOWDOWN
of a 1.39 ms frame. Those presets are `only_dct` and therefore take the
unchanged owned path; what they pay is the wrapper's extra call frame and
`grown_out`'s `is_empty` branch. `#[inline]` on the wrapper was tried against
exactly this and measured null-to-worse on all six gradient cells (256 p2
1.014x against 1.018x without it), so it is NOT in the tree. In absolute time
the trade is 5.8 ms/frame gained at gradient 512 p2 against 0.10 ms lost at
512 p6 and 0.04 ms at 512 p10.

The photo's -2.5 % at p2 tracks its -1.97 % Ir; the gradient is smaller because
its allocator traffic is 7x lighter (1,339x C against the photo's 9,296x,
`callcount_realimg_2026-09-04`), which is the whole reason this was measured on
real content.

MEMORY — the hard constraint of this chunk. Both quantities, both ISAs,
gradient qp 40 preset 13, `.obu` identical to the baseline on every row:

  aarch64 (this Mac), the inter cell, INTERLEAVED `mem_bisect.sh`, 21 rounds:
      base  median 142,128 KiB   min 140,160   max 160,464
      cand  median 142,144 KiB   min 140,112   max 142,384
    +16 KiB on the median, BELOW base on the min, and a tighter distribution.
    A `MB_THREADS=1` run (9 rounds) reads 142,128 -> 142,176.
  aarch64 `mem_peak.sh`, median of 5 (base -> cand, KiB): 1280 still
    28,176 -> 28,176, videokey 33,184 -> 33,280, inter 55,328 -> 55,328;
    2048 still 72,480 -> 72,528, videokey 87,616 -> 87,760, inter
    142,096 -> 142,256. x86_64 `mem_peak.sh`, median of 5: 1280 still
    29,112 -> 29,612, videokey 34,696 -> 34,700, inter 45,648 -> 45,092;
    2048 still 68,792 -> 68,620, videokey 77,944 -> 77,860, inter
    109,268 -> 109,584. Every one inside its own run-to-run band.
  x86_64 peak HEAP (heaptrack, LIVE bytes): 2048 still 61.07 -> 61.07 M,
    2048 inter 101.78 -> 101.78 M — identical, because the pooled buffers are
    only reachable on the multi-candidate path and preset 13 never takes it.

=================== FOUR VARIANTS MEASURED AND REJECTED ===================

Each was built, byte-checked and measured; none is in the tree. They are here
because two of them are the same arithmetic as the landed form and still cost
memory, which is the transferable finding.

  1. POOL EVERY TRIAL (no `only_dct` gate). Best instruction count of the four:
     p2 -2.00 % (47,462,759,437), allocator 15,142,201. But the aarch64 inter
     2048 cell went 142,112 -> 150,336 KiB median — +5.8 %, with the
     distributions NOT overlapping, reproduced at `MB_THREADS=1` (9 rounds) and
     at auto threads (11 and 21 rounds). x86 RSS and x86 peak heap were flat, so
     this is macOS `libmalloc` region retention responding to the size-class mix
     — the same phenomenon `mem_refclone_2026-09-04` decomposed with `vmmap`
     (~60 MiB of regions holding no live block). Cost: 0.03 pp of Ir to fix.
  2. C's LITERAL SELECT (`tx_type == DCT_DCT` owned, everything else pooled).
     Memory clean, but p2 only -1.42 % (47,744,675,928) and allocator
     16,706,945: when a non-DCT type wins, this pays BOTH the DCT trial's owned
     pair AND the winner's materialisation. Faithful to C's line, worse on the
     port's cost model, superseded by the `only_dct` split.
  3. PRE-SIZE THE BUFFERS IN THE CALLER (the wrapper allocates `vec![0i32;
     pw*ph]` / `vec![0u8; w*h]` itself, using `tx_unit_inner`'s own predicates,
     and hands them in warm). Identical sizes, identical counts, identical
     entry points, p2 -1.97 % — and the aarch64 inter 2048 median went
     142,128 -> 148,352 KiB (+4.4 %, 21 interleaved rounds). **The allocation
     POINT is what moved it**: pre-sizing makes both buffers live across the
     residual, the forward transform and the RDOQ instead of being created
     between them, and the live-set interleaving is what macOS's region
     retention keys on. The landed form allocates from `grown_out` at the
     original program point, which is why it is written the way it is.
  4. `grown_out`'s `resize` ON AN EMPTY BUFFER (instead of `vec![0; n]`).
     `Vec::resize` from zero is `__rust_alloc` + a zeroing loop, not `calloc`:
     +0.88 M `memset` calls and 2 M allocations moved from `calloc` to `malloc`,
     p2 -1.89 % instead of -1.97 %.

Also tried and not kept: `#[inline]` on the owned-output wrapper (above).

=================== BYTE IDENTITY AND GATES ===================

Every callgrind cell: identity pre-pass (port writes .yuv + .obu, C reads the
same .yuv, `cmp`) identical, AND each instrumented run's own .obu `cmp`'d
against it — 46,462 B at p2 and 45,688 B at p6, both sides, before and after.
Every `perf_ab` cell reports ident=Y. Every `mem_peak` / `mem_bisect` row
carries the same `obu_bytes` on both binaries.

aarch64 (this Mac, /opt/homebrew/bin/bash, one harness at a time):
  `cargo nextest run --workspace` 2530/2530, `regression_spotcheck` 104/104,
  `identity_full_8bit` 1100/1100 (+0 pinned, 0 harness errors), `inter_byte_gate`
  PASS (96 required, 0 failed, 1 known-open, 0 crashed, 0 harness errors),
  `video_key_matrix` 59/60 (the one diff is the known-open `gradient p0`,
  1341 vs 1342 B, unmoved), `fctx_gate` PASS (96/96 shared fields on both
  frames), `inter_decode_gate` 5/5 PASS, `inter_decode_census` 96/96 PASS,
  `inter_completion_scan` with `SCAN_GATE=1` 64 OK / 0 REFUSED / 0 CRASH PASS,
  `screen_palette_gate` 50/50 byte-identical (38 palette-coding cells).
x86_64 (r7900x, same tree): nextest 2540/2540, `regression_spotcheck` 104/104,
  `identity_full_8bit` 1100/1100, `inter_byte_gate` PASS (96/0/1).

ONE HARNESS TRAP, RECORDED BECAUSE IT COST A RED RUN: the gate chain exported
`ZENAV1_CORPUS_ROOT=~/work/zen` for `screen_palette_gate.sh` (whose
`lib_corpus.sh` wants the directory that CONTAINS the corpora), and
`tier_invariance::intrabc_output_is_tier_invariant_on_real_screen_content`
reads the same variable as the directory that contains `gb82-sc/graph.png`
— i.e. `~/work/zen/codec-corpus`. The test asserts the file exists rather than
skipping, so it failed loudly and correctly; the encoder was never involved.
Two consumers, one variable, two different meanings of "root".
